nique among the pages of its page type", so the two cannot both be `module/badge-variant`. A `text-property` page at `temper/temper-progress/activity-categories/properties/badge-variant.text-property.ts:8` also carries the slug `badge-variant`, which is allowed because it is a different page type.\n\nWHAT I DID NOT ESTABLISH. I did not test the refusal by attempting the rename; the slug collision above is read off the two module pages and the uniqueness rule rather than observed as a refusal message. I did not judge which union is the right one to keep, nor whether the narrow one\'s eight are narrow on purpose — `color-rule-variant.module.ts:7` defines its module as "the named colors a badge is drawn in and a color rule answers", which is consistent with a color-only vocabulary being deliberate. I did not measure whether any value outside the narrow eight ever reaches the components that read it.',
